- How would you extend to a third task with a different label delay?
- How would you validate drift alarms in production and trigger retraining bursts?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical NLP pipeline setup, handling class imbalance, and real-world deployment concerns for a beginner-friendly problem.

## Key Concepts
- TF-IDF vectorization with unigrams/bigrams
- Handling imbalanced data via class_weight
- Time-based train/test splits to mimic streaming data
- Evaluation: macro F1 and PR-AUC for imbalanced tasks
- Canary rollout and monitoring basics for production safety

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: outline of pipeline components
function buildPipeline(){
  const vectorizer = new TFIDF({ngramRange:[1,2], maxFeatures:100000});
  const model = new LogisticRegression({classWeight:'balanced'});
  return {vectorizer, model};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend to multi-class categorization of spam types?
- How would you monitor drift and adjust thresholds in production?

## Why This Is Asked
This checks practical CV setup, leakage awareness, and model selection on small data.

## Key Concepts
- Data leakage prevention
- Stratified cross-validation
- Pipeline preprocessing
- Model comparison metrics (AUROC, calibration)

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: stratified K-fold CV in JS-like syntax
const k = 5;
const folds = stratifiedKFoldSplit(labels, k);
for (const [trainIdx, testIdx] of folds) {
  const model = trainLogisticRegression(features[trainIdx], labels[trainIdx]);
  const preds = model.predictProba(features[testIdx]);
  console.log(rocAuc(labels[testIdx], preds));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle class imbalance if AUROC is similar across models?
- How could you incorporate feature engineering without leaking future information?

## Why This Is Asked
Production anomaly systems face non-stationarity, sparse labels, and strict latency. This question tests end-to-end design, from data schema to deployment, plus practical techniques like self-supervised pretraining and online adaptation.

## Key Concepts
- Self-supervised pretraining for unlabeled streams
- Online adaptation with meta-learning
- Two-tower architecture for heterogeneous features
- Drift detection and safe rollout/rollback
- Latency budgeting and quantization

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example gating logic for latency-adaptive routing
function route(payload, limitMs) {
  const t0 = performance.now();
  const score = computeScore(payload);
  const dt = performance.now() - t0;
  if (dt > limitMs) return 'fallback';
  return score;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you evaluate drift detectors in an AB test?
- What failure modes could cause late anomaly alerts and how to mitigate?
